  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICRC humanitarian action in Ethiopia 2022-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This allocation contributes to achieving the objectives of the International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC)&#x2019;s Ethiopia Country Appeal for 2022. The ICRC&apos;s activities in Ethiopia focus on:
&#x2022;	Delivering food assistance, relief, and essential services where they are most needed
&#x2022;	Urging protection for people affected by violence
&#x2022;	Bolstering the delivery of life-saving health care
&#x2022;	Enabling people to meet urgent needs and restore their livelihoods
&#x2022;	Increasing access to clean water
&#x2022;	Restoring family links
&#x2022;	Supporting improved treatment and living conditions for detainees
Ethiopia faces a combination of severe humanitarian challenges, including drought, internal armed conflict, cholera outbreaks, and soaring prices for food and fertiliser. The recent peace agreement between the government and armed opposition groups has enabled greater humanitarian access, particularly in the northern regions, allowing for an expanded response.</narrative>
  </description>
